[0.048, "o", "{\r\n    \"classification\": \"application_regression\",\r\n    \"reasoning\": \"The test failure is caused by a parameter name mismatch between the frontend and backend. The pagination component in the template generates URLs with the parameter 'page-size' (lowercase with hyphen), but the backend route in home.py expects 'PAGE_SIZE' (uppercase with underscore) on line 32. When the test selects a page size of 10, the URL updates correctly to include '?page-size=10', but the backend fails to read this parameter and defaults to showing 25 items per page. Since the database only contains 14 photos, all 14 are displayed instead of the expected 10. This was verified by manually testing with the correct parameter name 'PAGE_SIZE=10', which correctly displayed only 10 photos. The test code is correct and uses proper Playwright selectors. The test run history shows this test passed on Feb 14 earlier in the day but failed in the most recent run, suggesting a recent code change introduced this regression.\",\r\n    \"affectedTests\": "]
[0.000, "o", "[\r\n        \"Photo Gallery Feature \\u203a gallery_page_navigation_works - Verify that the page navigation works\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"suggestedAction\": \"Fix the parameter name mismatch in the backend. Change line 32 in /Users/jason.turan/projects/yaffo/yaffo/routes/home.py from `page_size = request.args.get('PAGE_SIZE', type=int)` to `page_size = request.args.get('page-size', type=int)` to match the parameter name used by the pagination component template.\"\r\n}\r\n"]
